{"id": "EUVD-2026-49599", "enisaUuid": "01762cdf-d0fb-3212-90ea-a7a9e36ea49a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf, sockmap: reject overflowing copy + len in bpf_msg_push_data()\n\nWhen the scatterlist ring is full or nearly full, bpf_msg_push_data()\nenters a copy fallback path and computes copy + len for the page\nallocation size. Since len comes from BPF with arg3_type = ARG_ANYTHING\nand both are u32, a crafted len can wrap the sum to a small value,\ncausing an undersized allocation followed by an out-of-bounds memcpy.\n\n BUG: unable to handle page fault for address: ffffed104089a402\n Oops: Oops: 0000 [#1] SMP KASAN NOPTI\n Call Trace:\n  __asan_memcpy (mm/kasan/shadow.c:105)\n  bpf_msg_push_data (net/core/filter.c:2852 net/core/filter.c:2788)\n  bpf_prog_9ed8b5711920a7d7+0x2e/0x36\n  sk_psock_msg_verdict (net/core/skmsg.c:934)\n  tcp_bpf_sendmsg (net/ipv4/tcp_bpf.c:421 net/ipv4/tcp_bpf.c:584)\n  __sys_sendto (net/socket.c:2206)\n  do_syscall_64 (arch/x86/entry/syscall_64.c:94)\n  entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe (arch/x86/entry/entry_64.S:130)\n\nAdd an overflow check before the allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-07-27T20:10:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:40", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1644c9508d24f50dd9e8ebe8d3ba86e0996d2f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a12b1575f9feabd91695a9e9d004862f7195fa25", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff39d0e3b4feeb65ca43c453d7c75fdf872ded0d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/888706a76286c547bd035432602571e8024b5305", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db77b6bb6e6edb79b10b4efcce346eec5582d588", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e40056bb5c829f0423f0a6694a0477726d2147e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd004716ba75fed6d185795c85cdc92540ebeaab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c0a8ed85349dae298712d79cb276acfeb794d82"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v3w7-wgcw-wjf2", "CVE-2026-64548"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01753fc0-6879-32f7-9a4d-34a67cbbb0a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6fff607e2f14bd7c63c06c464a6f93b8efbabe28 <db77b6bb6e6edb79b10b4efcce346eec5582d588"}, {"id": "04cc874f-fb9e-32c8-b7b0-9dd604bd030c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6fff607e2f14bd7c63c06c464a6f93b8efbabe28 <ff39d0e3b4feeb65ca43c453d7c75fdf872ded0d"}, {"id": "0afbe579-9320-3fdd-b82d-df6a4f4bd781", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6fff607e2f14bd7c63c06c464a6f93b8efbabe28 <4e40056bb5c829f0423f0a6694a0477726d2147e"}, {"id": "1e12f81b-3661-3e1e-bcc8-b59a16d98e02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "25aecad9-10e4-3778-a175-fa67115d2318", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.20"}, {"id": "25f32159-00a8-30fe-b826-f308ba0d7aa7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6fff607e2f14bd7c63c06c464a6f93b8efbabe28 <a12b1575f9feabd91695a9e9d004862f7195fa25"}, {"id": "3eab1a1f-63ca-3705-bdd7-f1cb5d5a7433", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "3f98d202-0a93-3d4d-ba84-a4c0920ceb67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "4f564a91-4632-32f0-81df-80c0784bc0b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6fff607e2f14bd7c63c06c464a6f93b8efbabe28 <f1644c9508d24f50dd9e8ebe8d3ba86e0996d2f5"}, {"id": "5023cef4-166a-377d-8995-f2a1ede4e32d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6fff607e2f14bd7c63c06c464a6f93b8efbabe28 <888706a76286c547bd035432602571e8024b5305"}, {"id": "7acea338-a3f9-3cd8-82ed-c603697f134d", "product": {"name": "Lin